## ***********************************************************************
## **
## **  GUI2.PLAIN.INC.BL -- GUI.LISTBOX, unbanked.
## **
## **      GUI.LISTBOX
## **
## **  A .BODY name is not an accident and not a rename waiting to happen: a
## **  banked routine cannot select its own bank, so the public name has to be
## **  a label in low memory and the code has to be a label of its own. This
## **  file is that public name for a program that does NOT bank -- the same
## **  eighteen entry points LIB.GUIBANK.INC.BL provides, minus the BANK.
## **
## **  ONE FILE PER MODULE, and that is the same split LIB.GUIBANK.INC.BL and
## **  LIB.FUTILBANK.INC.BL make, for the same reason: BASLOAD resolves every
## **  label in every file it reads, so a shim for a module you did not
## **  #INCLUDE stops the build with LABEL NOT FOUND. One file holding all
## **  eighteen would make a MENUVERT test carry the whole GUI.
## **
## **  NEVER BOTH. LIB.GUIBANK.INC.BL defines these same labels, so a program
## **  that banks the library must not #INCLUDE this one -- BASLOAD stops with
## **  DUPLICATE SYMBOL. Bank the library or run it from low memory; the
## **  callers read identically either way, which is the point of the split.
## **
## **  ITS OWN FILE, because GUI2.INC.BL is its own #INCLUDE: nothing else in
## **  the library wants a set of marks, and a program with no listbox should
## **  not carry one.
## **
## **  WARNING: no include guard in here, and GUI2.INC.BL has none either, for
## **  the same reason -- BASLOAD rejects a digit in a #IFNDEF name, so
## **  GUI2.PLAIN.DEFS is INVALID PARAMETER. #INCLUDE this once.
## **
## **  REQUIRES, and does not #INCLUDE for you:
## **      GUI2.INC.BL       the body
## **      GUI.INC.BL        the listbox is a dialog around GUI.FORM, and it
## **                        opens and closes its box through GUI.OPEN and
## **                        GUI.CLOSE, so GUI.PLAIN.INC.BL is wanted too
## **
## ***********************************************************************
GOTO GUI2.PLAIN.MODULE.END

GUI.LISTBOX:   GOSUB GUI.LISTBOX.BODY : RETURN

GUI2.PLAIN.MODULE.END:
